Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Exercises 1.4 ", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"557e6f7f-6fa5-4e1a-bb02-e9b930d3cdb2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1.4.1 pg 12 (with modifications)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"057ab79e-b80d-4aff-b923-f170ea364ad3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part 1:  A raindrop falls from a cloud and is subject to a constant \
gravitational force.  Air resistance provides viscous damping, but there is \
no restoring force. Formulate and use ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to solve the resulting differential equation (without initial conditions) \
that models this situation and interpret the solution.  (Hint:   Use Example \
1.3, Equation 1.5 on page 5 (with k = 0))."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"eda2c633-0087-4b98-ba80-da46fcaaf8ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part 2:  Also, use ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to find the solution corresponding to the initial conditions: ",
 StyleBox["y[0] = y0,  y'[0] = v0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"50f0e3ba-3dcd-4e0d-afaf-3d009e47fea4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part 3: Extract the solution y[t] from the replacement rule found in Part \
2.  Plot (on separate graphs) the specific solution y[t] from Part 2 and plot \
the velocity y'[t] corresponding to conditions:\n",
 StyleBox["\tg = 32.2\n\tm = .02\n\tk1 = .003\n\ty0 = 10,000\n\tv0 = 0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n until the raindrop reaches the ground (i.e. y[t] = 0). "
}], "Text",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"e75805c8-5cba-4053-892d-8f1a0b76fff1"],

Cell["\<\
Part 4: About how long is required for the raindrop to reach the ground?  \
(Use your graphs to estimate this quantity).\
\>", "Text",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"d59eef6b-79c4-4dbc-8240-ca9b77ed2d2d"],

Cell["\<\
Part 5: Also, use the function y[t] to precisely solve this non-algebraic \
equation for the time, t1, at which the raindrop strikes the ground.\
\>", "Text",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"901d7a44-8947-4309-abc2-93ce04ef5293"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part 6: Finally, use the ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " Limit command to determine the limiting velocity (i.e. terminal velocity) \
as t\[Rule]\[Infinity] and compare this limiting value to y'[t1] (which \
corresponds to the velocity that the rain drop strikes the ground).\nHint: \
Remember to simplify your intermediate results."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"3d3238b0-51b3-49fd-969a-3bd7863ff794"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1.4.2 pg 12 (with modifications)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4cf2898f-7b94-46dc-8d0b-b8837d4990b0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A spherical rain drop evaporates at a (volumetric) rate that is \
proportional to its surface area.  If r is the rain drop radius, then v is \
proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["r", "3"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "80d9fc69-e674-4fde-9479-1b519baf4b94"],
 " while the surface area is proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["r", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5fbcacc8-99a2-45a8-90af-eb08c39fe7c2"],
 ". Use the symbolic capability of ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to find an expression for the volume v of the drop as a function of time \
by solving a suitable ordinary differential equation.  Hint: To evaluate the \
constants of integration, set the initial condition ",
 StyleBox["v[0] = v0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"e8dd3125-ccbe-4e72-bd19-5060e140a185"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1.4.3 pg 13 (with modifications)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"44655808-57ae-4224-b1e3-be7737d3c97a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Water enters a cylindrical tank at a constant rate (volume per unit time, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Qin",
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"38d7ff6c-9bbf-4a95-9bb1-98f5c95e8048"],
 ").  The tank has a hole in the bottom and so water flows out through it.  \
Let h be the depth of the water in the tank.  It is known from Bernoulli's \
principal that the rate at which water flows through the hole (i.e. \
volumetric rate out, ",
 StyleBox["Qout[t]",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", in volume per unit time) is proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["h",
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1cc74ff9-c756-407d-bc52-ca10a40d13f0"],
 ".  Suppose the tank has a constant cross-sectional area A.  Find a \
differential equation for h.  Use ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to solve the resulting differential equation symbolically.  Determine the \
equilibrium state and discuss whether it is stable or not (see example 1.5 in \
the text). (Hint: Set the initial height of water in the tank to h0, i.e. \
h[0] = h0.)"
}], "Text",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"48f4f571-2211-4582-959f-9184a93aa3eb"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["# 6 (not in book)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9a416cf5-5158-4964-8d8a-6a104473a372"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part 1:    Solve:  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"z", "'"}], "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"r", "*", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"z", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "*", 
       RowBox[{"z", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], " ", "=", " ", "0"}],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dd068f3e-94da-4ad0-acbc-f4e8fded88d4"],
 "  subject to the initial conditions:  ",
 StyleBox["z[0] = z0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "  and ",
 StyleBox["z'[0] = 0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ".\n\nPart 2: Extract the solution as a function z[t] using replacement \
rules found in Part 1.\n\nPart 3: Using the Limit command, show that as r\
\[Rule]0 one recoveries the solution ",
 StyleBox["{z0 Cos[t \[Omega]]}",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ".  (Hint, to simplify the result of your limit use FullSimplify rather than \
just Simplify)."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"94df407f-be54-46dd-b567-27fc42cd8628"]
}, Closed]]
}, Open  ]]
},
WindowSize->{841, 538},
WindowMargins->{{1, Automatic}, {Automatic, 4}},
